---
source: crates/mori-checker/src/tests.rs
description: "Code:\n\nprofile \"moriarty-beta/1\";\nagreement Family {\n  domain Preview = { id: \"preview\", chain: \"midnight\", network: \"preview\" };\n  domain Other = { id: \"other\", chain: \"midnight\", network: \"other\" };\n  asset USD = { domain: Preview, id: \"usd\", scale: 2, representation: \"native\" };\n  asset GOLD = { domain: Preview, id: \"gold\", scale: 3, representation: \"native\" };\n  account alice = { domain: Preview, id: \"alice\" };\n  pool amm = { domain: Preview, id: \"amm\", assets: [USD, GOLD] };\n  intent swap = {\n    operation: amm.swap_exact_input(\n      pool: amm, owner: alice, input: 10 USD, output_asset: GOLD,\n      net_floor: 1 GOLD, fee_cap: 0.1 USD,\n    ),\n    asset: USD,\n    net_floor: 1 USD,\n    valid: [0, 10, 20],\n  };\n  intent out = {\n    operation: bridge.escrow(owner: alice, amount: 5 USD, destination: Other, claim_id: \"c\"),\n    asset: GOLD,\n    domain: Other,\n  };\n}\n"
---
mori::check::wrong_asset

  × `net_floor` must be a `GOLD` amount because a swap's floor is measured in
  │ its `output_asset`, but it is a `USD` amount.
    ╭─[test.mori:15:16]
 14 │     asset: USD,
 15 │     net_floor: 1 USD,
    ·                ──┬──
    ·                  ╰── a `USD` amount
 16 │     valid: [0, 10, 20],
    ╰────

mori::check::invalid_validity

  × An intent's `valid` must be a `rounds(...)` window or two round numbers.
    ╭─[test.mori:16:12]
 15 │     net_floor: 1 USD,
 16 │     valid: [0, 10, 20],
    ·            ─────┬─────
    ·                 ╰── not a round window
 17 │   };
    ╰────
  help: For example:

            valid: rounds(domain: Preview, from: 0, to: 100),
            valid: [0, 100],

mori::check::different_domains

  × `owner` is on `Preview`, but `domain` is on `Other`.
    ╭─[test.mori:19:37]
 18 │   intent out = {
 19 │     operation: bridge.escrow(owner: alice, amount: 5 USD, destination: Other, claim_id: "c"),
    ·                                     ──┬──
    ·                                       ╰── on `Preview`
 20 │     asset: GOLD,
 21 │     domain: Other,
    ·             ──┬──
    ·               ╰── on `Other`
 22 │   };
    ╰────
  help: Everything an operation touches must be on one domain.

mori::check::different_domains

  × `amount` is on `Preview`, but `domain` is on `Other`.
    ╭─[test.mori:19:52]
 18 │   intent out = {
 19 │     operation: bridge.escrow(owner: alice, amount: 5 USD, destination: Other, claim_id: "c"),
    ·                                                    ──┬──
    ·                                                      ╰── on `Preview`
 20 │     asset: GOLD,
 21 │     domain: Other,
    ·             ──┬──
    ·               ╰── on `Other`
 22 │   };
    ╰────
  help: Everything an operation touches must be on one domain.

mori::check::different_domains

  × `asset` is on `Preview`, but `domain` is on `Other`.
    ╭─[test.mori:20:12]
 19 │     operation: bridge.escrow(owner: alice, amount: 5 USD, destination: Other, claim_id: "c"),
 20 │     asset: GOLD,
    ·            ──┬─
    ·              ╰── on `Preview`
 21 │     domain: Other,
    ·             ──┬──
    ·               ╰── on `Other`
 22 │   };
    ╰────
  help: Everything an operation touches must be on one domain.

mori::check::wrong_intent_asset

  × The intent's `asset` is `GOLD`, but the bridge moves its `amount`, which
  │ is in `USD`.
    ╭─[test.mori:20:12]
 19 │     operation: bridge.escrow(owner: alice, amount: 5 USD, destination: Other, claim_id: "c"),
 20 │     asset: GOLD,
    ·            ──┬─
    ·              ╰── `GOLD`
 21 │     domain: Other,
    ╰────
